  "description": "The target audience is individuals who hold or are susceptible to Islamophobic and anti-refugee stereotypes, particularly those who believe refugees are inherently violent or dangerous. The meme is designed to appeal to people who distrust or fear refugees, often conflated with Muslim populations, by using imagery of civil unrest and text that frames refugees as a threat to societal order. This audience is likely to be receptive to hateful narratives that dehumanize refugees and justify prejudice or hostility toward them.",
